# Tutorial 11 — DXF, IFC, OBJ/GLB and CSV schedules; importing IFC back.
title: Import and export
summary: DXF, IFC, OBJ and GLB export, schedules to CSV and IFC import
---
open sample "Cedar House"
caption "DXF" "EXPORT DXF: the plan for AutoCAD and other CAD software"
type EXPORT DXF $TMP/Cedar-House.dxf
wait 1.5
caption "IFC" "EXPORT IFC: walls, slabs, doors, windows and spaces for BIM software"
type EXPORT IFC $TMP/Cedar-House.ifc
wait 1.5
caption "3D models" "OBJ and GLB for 3D software, game engines and the web"
type EXPORT OBJ $TMP/Cedar-House.obj
type EXPORT GLB $TMP/Cedar-House.glb
wait 1.5
caption "Schedules" "SCHEDULE builds tables of doors, windows, rooms and walls"
type SCHEDULE Doors ;
wait 2
type SCHEDULE Rooms ;
wait 2
caption "Schedules to CSV" "EXPORT CSV writes the schedules for spreadsheets"
type EXPORT CSV $TMP/Cedar-House-schedules.csv
wait 1.5
caption "Importing IFC" "IFCIMPORT reads IFC into native, editable elements"
open new
type IFCIMPORT $TMP/Cedar-House.ifc
escape
zoom extents
wait 2
click mode 3D
wait 1
type SEISO
orbit 50 4
wait 1
click mode 2D
caption "Also: DWG, Rhino, SketchUp, STEP, PDF…" "File ▸ Import and IMPORTFILE accept many more formats"
wait 3.5
